## 7. Output examples

Medi-Cal only:

```
O: Medi-Cal
P: GENSERV_MEDICAL
Q:
R: unknown
```

Medi-Cal (SSI/SSP), SSI, IEP and school speech:

```
O: Medi-Cal (SSI/SSP), SSI – Supplemental Security Income, K–12 School / School District – IEP, SELPA – Language/Speech Therapy
P: GENSERV_MEDICAL, GENSERV_SSI_SSDI, GENSERV_IEP, GENSERV_SPEECH_OT_PT
Q:
R: CHOC
```

Private insurer plus counseling and WIC:

```
O: Cigna, Individual Counselling, WIC (Food Assist)
P: GENSERV_OTHER, GENSERV_FOODASSIST
Q: Cigna, Individual Counselling
R:
```

## 8. Writing and verification (Google Sheets via browser)

- Cells with data validation reject typed text. Select the top-left target cell (Name box), then dispatch a synthetic paste of tab-separated values (columns O, P, Q, R), one row per line.
- Verify by fetching the sheet as CSV (`/gviz/tq?tqx=out:csv&gid=<gid>`) and comparing to the expected values. Sheet row = CSV index + 2.
- Never write column N.

## 9. Do not

- Do not use IFSP plans, client logs or progress reports as the source.
- Do not add planned, pending or declined services.
- Do not infer services that are not written in the IPP/CDER.
- Do not put client names, UCI numbers or case details in this file or anything derived from it.
